From: Rob Clark <robin.clark@oss.qualcomm.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/gem: Validate lazy VM in GEM_NEW

Otherwise creating a _NO_SHARE BO before any BOs are mapped could cause
a NPE.

Reported-by: Sashiko <sashiko-bot@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Rob Clark <robin.clark@oss.qualcomm.com>
Patchwork: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/743104/
Message-ID: <20260729155609.20190-14-robin.clark@oss.qualcomm.com>
(cherry picked from commit a6d87a272b2c8fe1366ea9a8e2e4cccddbb4157f)
[Akisaira: v7.2 lacks the preceding df68029e639b ("drm/msm/gem: Set resv
 before exposing obj"), so msm_gem_new_handle() still reads ctx->vm
 directly after creating the object. Look the VM up with msm_context_vm()
 and validate it before msm_gem_new() instead, which is where upstream
 ends up; the resv race fixed by df68029e639b is not part of this.]
Origin: backport, https://git.kernel.org/torvalds/c/a6d87a272b2c8fe1366ea9a8e2e4cccddbb4157f
Upstream-Status: Backport [v7.3-rc1, a6d87a272b2c]
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.c | 18 +++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.c
index efd3d3c9a..af14a6c42 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.c
@@ -1134,9 +1134,20 @@ int msm_gem_new_handle(struct drm_device *dev, struct drm_file *file,
 		size_t size, uint32_t flags, uint32_t *handle,
 		char *name)
 {
-	struct drm_gem_object *obj;
+	struct drm_gem_object *obj, *r_obj = NULL;
 	int ret;
 
+	if (flags & MSM_BO_NO_SHARE) {
+		struct msm_drm_private *priv = dev->dev_private;
+		struct msm_context *ctx = file->driver_priv;
+		struct drm_gpuvm *vm = msm_context_vm(dev, ctx);
+
+		if (!priv->gpu || !vm)
+			return UERR(EINVAL, dev, "not supported with shared VM");
+
+		r_obj = drm_gpuvm_resv_obj(vm);
+	}
+
 	obj = msm_gem_new(dev, size, flags);
 
 	if (IS_ERR(obj))
@@ -1145,10 +1156,7 @@ int msm_gem_new_handle(struct drm_device *dev, struct drm_file *file,
 	if (name)
 		msm_gem_object_set_name(obj, "%s", name);
 
-	if (flags & MSM_BO_NO_SHARE) {
-		struct msm_context *ctx = file->driver_priv;
-		struct drm_gem_object *r_obj = drm_gpuvm_resv_obj(ctx->vm);
-
+	if (r_obj) {
 		drm_gem_object_get(r_obj);
 
 		obj->resv = r_obj->resv;
